When their hands are opposite each other, they are $12$ inches apart, which is exactly equal to $1$ yard. Each passing of the ball from one ball to the other is $1$ yard. The first pass occurred $12x + 1 > 1024x$ seconds before it is completed. This leads us to we solve $12x + 1 = 1024x$ to get $1 = 1012x$. This gives us $x = \boxed{1/1012}$. In other words, it took $1/1012$ seconds for the ball to complete its journey. So, $x$ should be $\boxed{506}$.



